{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":504096,"name":"Shaun Bowe","username":"Shaun_Bowe","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/shaun_bowe/{size}/120884_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-30T16:27:28.008Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504096-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504096-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504096-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504096-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen trying to “Login with Google” as a service account Grok Bot opens the Google Popup correctly, enters the username or selects it from a list. Then when it is time to enter the password it refuses to enter the password even though 1Password has it. I asked for details on why and this is what the bot said: \"I don’t have the password. 1Password keeps it, and the fill into that Google popup was rejected twice. The page is a small sign-in window on top of Ramp, and the filler only accepts a full sign-in form. It said this window doesn’t qualify, so nothing was typed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe screen is yours so you can fill it from the Google item. Hand it back when you’re in.\"\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504096-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504096-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAttempt to Login to a website using GrokBot that uses Login with Google.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504096-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504096-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot completes the login using 1Password\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504096-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504096-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOther\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504096-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504096-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrokBot: 0.63.0\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504096-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504096-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSometimes - I can sometimes use Cursor\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-30T16:55:18.761Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":13,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":65.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":173423,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-wont-login-to-google-account-using-1password","display_username":"Shaun Bowe","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":137805,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-wont-login-to-google-account-using-1password/173423/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":504140,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-30T16:48:01.117Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the report. What you’re seeing is that Grok Bot gets to the password step in the Google popup and can’t fill it from 1Password. This is an issue we’re tracking. I shared your report with the team.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor now, the workaround is to sign in to Google manually once on the bot screen:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhen the bot hands you control of the screen, type the password yourself from your Google item in 1Password.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eComplete 2-step verification if Google asks.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHand control back to the bot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe bot’s browser usually keeps that Google session, so the next Sign in with Google should only ask you to pick an account, without the password step.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo help us investigate, which email is your Grok Bot signed in with (if it’s different from your forum email), and roughly when did this happen?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-30T16:48:01.117Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":5.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":173423,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-wont-login-to-google-account-using-1password","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":75